  "term": "postmortem examination",
  "definition": "A postmortem examination is an inspection of a body after death to identify the main diseases, injuries, or other conditions present and help determine likely causes of death. In this source, it refers to necropsy findings used to describe common fatal conditions in sheep and goats.",
